<BaseLayout title="Acupressure for Fertility: Points Used to Support Reproductive Health" description="Acupressure points traditionally used to support reproductive health and cycles, including SP6, CV4, CV6, ST36, and GV20. Evidence and safety notes included." breadcrumbs={[{ "label": "Home", "href": "/" }, { "label": "Conditions", "href": "/conditions/" }, { "label": "Acupressure for Fertility", "href": "/conditions/acupressure-for-fertility/" }]} datePublished="2026-08-27" dateModified="2026-08-27" articleSchema={true}>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 lg:px-6"><h1 class="mb-4">Acupressure for Fertility: Points Used to Support Reproductive Health</h1><p class="text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 text-lg mb-8">In traditional Chinese medicine, a set of lower-abdomen and lower-leg points is used to support the reproductive system and regulate the menstrual cycle. Some people use these alongside fertility care. This guide explains the points and keeps the expectations realistic: acupressure is a supportive practice, not a treatment for infertility.</p><div class="mb-8 p-4 bg-forest-50 dark:bg-forest-900/20 border-l-4 border-forest-500 rounded-r-lg"><p class="text-sm text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300"><strong>Research Note:</strong> Acupuncture and acupressure for fertility are studied mostly in the context of assisted reproduction, with mixed and preliminary findings. The evidence does not show that acupressure alone treats infertility. Use it only as a complement to care from a fertility specialist.</p></div><section id="cv4" class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4"><a href="/points/cv4-guanyuan-acupressure-point/" class="text-forest-600 hover:text-forest-500 dark:text-forest-300">1. CV4 (Guanyuan) - Gate of Origin</a></h2><p class="mb-3">CV4 on the lower abdomen is a foundational point traditionally used to nourish reproductive and pelvic energy.</p><p class="mb-3"><strong>Location:</strong> On the midline of the lower abdomen, about three finger-widths below the navel. <a href="/points/cv4-guanyuan-acupressure-point/">CV4 guide</a>.</p><p class="mb-3"><strong>Technique:</strong> Lie down and press gently in slow circles for 2-3 minutes. Warm the hands or use a heating pad for comfort.</p></section><section id="cv6" class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4"><a href="/points/cv6-qihai-acupressure-point/" class="text-forest-600 hover:text-forest-500 dark:text-forest-300">2. CV6 (Qihai) - Sea of Qi</a></h2><p class="mb-3">CV6 sits just above CV4 and is traditionally used to strengthen the lower abdomen and support cycle regularity.</p><p class="mb-3"><strong>Location:</strong> On the midline of the lower abdomen, about two finger-widths below the navel. <a href="/points/cv6-qihai-acupressure-point/">CV6 guide</a>.</p><p class="mb-3"><strong>Technique:</strong> Gentle circular pressure for 2-3 minutes, breathing slowly.</p></section><section id="sp6" class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4"><a href="/points/sp6-sanyinjiao-acupressure-point/" class="text-forest-600 hover:text-forest-500 dark:text-forest-300">3. SP6 (Sanyinjiao) - Three Yin Intersection</a></h2><p class="mb-3">SP6, where three lower meridians meet, is one of the most-used points for menstrual and reproductive health in TCM.</p><p class="mb-3"><strong>Location:</strong> On the inside of the lower leg, about four finger-widths above the inner ankle bone. <a href="/points/sp6-sanyinjiao-acupressure-point/">SP6 guide</a>.</p><p class="mb-3"><strong>Technique:</strong> Press firmly for 2-3 minutes on each leg. Avoid during pregnancy.</p></section><section id="st36" class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4"><a href="/points/st36-zusanli-acupressure-point/" class="text-forest-600 hover:text-forest-500 dark:text-forest-300">4. ST36 (Zusanli) - Leg Three Miles</a></h2><p class="mb-3">ST36 supports digestion and overall vitality, which TCM views as foundational to reproductive health.</p><p class="mb-3"><strong>Location:</strong> About four finger-widths below the kneecap, one finger-width outward from the shinbone. <a href="/points/st36-zusanli-acupressure-point/">ST36 guide</a>.</p><p class="mb-3"><strong>Technique:</strong> Press firmly for 2-3 minutes on each leg.</p></section><section id="gv20" class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4"><a href="/points/gv20-baihui-acupressure-point/" class="text-forest-600 hover:text-forest-500 dark:text-forest-300">5. GV20 (Baihui) - Hundred Meetings</a></h2><p class="mb-3">GV20 at the crown is traditionally used to lift and balance energy and to ease the stress that often accompanies fertility journeys.</p><p class="mb-3"><strong>Location:</strong> On the midline of the head, about two finger-widths behind the hairline at the top of the skull. <a href="/points/gv20-baihui-acupressure-point/">GV20 guide</a>.</p><p class="mb-3"><strong>Technique:</strong> Gentle steady pressure with the fingertips for 1-2 minutes.</p></section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-3">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class="space-y-4"><details class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-stone-800 dark:bg-stone-900"><summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Can acupressure treat infertility?</summary><p class="mt-2 text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">No. It is a supportive practice that some people use alongside medical fertility care. If you have been trying to conceive for a year (or six months if over 35), see a fertility specialist for proper evaluation.</p></details><details class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-stone-800 dark:bg-stone-900"><summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Is it safe while trying to conceive?</summary><p class="mt-2 text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">The points here are traditionally used to support the cycle, but SP6, CV4, and CV6 are also points to approach with care in early pregnancy. If you are pregnant or think you might be, review our pregnancy safety guide and check with your provider before using abdominal points.</p></details></div></section><hr class="my-8"><div class="bg-stone-100 dark:bg-stone-800 rounded-lg p-6 text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400"><p><strong>Medical Disclaimer:</strong> This content is for informational purposes only and is not medical advice. Acupressure is not a treatment for infertility. Consult a qualified healthcare provider for fertility concerns.</p></div></article>
</BaseLayout>
